-- The exhibit for the DMN 1.3 exporter (Track D1 of the Lexipedia-superset
-- programme). Modelled on the decision logic of Regulation Crowdfunding that
-- the Lexipedia page draws as BPMN *gateways* -- which is the category error
-- the programme is about: eligibility and the investor limit are decisions, and
-- a decision belongs in a decision table.
--
-- Four decisions, deliberately of four different shapes, so the golden shows
-- every outcome the exporter has at once:
--
--   * `is accredited investor` -- U hit policy over a CONSIDER, OTHERWISE as
--                                 the <defaultOutputEntry>;
--   * `combined resources`     -- not a guarded chain at all, so a
--                                 <literalExpression> plus a fidelity note;
--   * `annual limit basis`     -- an IF/THEN/ELSE whose guard has no constant
--                                 endpoint, so a boolean column plus a note;
--   * `investor limit`         -- F hit policy over overlapping guards, with a
--                                 computed output entry on the last rule.
--
-- Figures are illustrative. The point of the exhibit is the SHAPE, not the
-- currency of the numbers.

ASSUME `annual income` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `net worth` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Investor Class`
  IS ONE OF
    `accredited`
    `retail`
    `institutional`

ASSUME `class` IS A `Investor Class`

-- A CONSIDER over distinct nullary constructors: the guards cannot both hold,
-- so the table is honestly Unique and OTHERWISE becomes the default output.
-- FEEL has no sum types, so the constructors serialise as strings.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is accredited investor` IF
  CONSIDER `class`
  WHEN `accredited`    THEN TRUE
  WHEN `institutional` THEN TRUE
  OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Not a guarded chain: plain arithmetic. DMN's own answer for logic with no
-- table shape is a boxed literal expression, and the fidelity report says so
-- rather than the exporter quietly dropping the decision.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`combined resources` MEANS
  `annual income` PLUS `net worth`

-- A guard comparing two VARIABLES. There is no constant endpoint to put in a
-- cell, so the conjunct becomes its own boolean column -- correct, and reported.
-- Guessing an endpoint here is what the exporter refuses to do.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`annual limit basis` MEANS
  IF `annual income` AT LEAST `net worth` THEN `net worth` ELSE `annual income`

-- Overlapping numeric thresholds in descending order: first match wins, so the
-- hit policy is F and no rule restates that an earlier one did not fire. The
-- last output entry is COMPUTED, which is legal DMN 8.2.9 and outside the
-- fragment DMN's analysis is defined over -- exactly the loss the report names.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`investor limit` MEANS
  BRANCH
    IF `is accredited investor`              THEN 100000000
    IF `annual limit basis` LESS THAN 124000 THEN 2500
    OTHERWISE `annual limit basis` * 10 / 100
